    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d24-a1">

                <pb facs="0113" n="25" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg25"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Mariscal to Mr. Clayton.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-10-05"><hi rendition="#italic">October 5,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Ambassador</hi>: In reply to your excellency’s
                    note of the 3d instant requesting data concerning the neutrality proclamations
                    issued by the Government of Mexico during the war between Russia and Japan, I
                    have the honor to transmit herewith two copies of the Diario Oficial, wherein
                    Mexico’s official declaration of neutrality in the Russian-Japanese conflict
                    appears. I renew, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Igno. Mariscal.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
